As previously indicated, as part of the tenure and promotion process
each year, the Dean of Faculties prepares a booklet for all faculty who
are being recommended for tenure and/or promotion which includes a
brief biographical sketch and a photograph.  Attached for your review is
a draft biographical paragraph we have prepared from information and
reports in your tenure and promotion file.  If you have any changes to
recommend, please contact Carolyn Jaros  (carolyn@science.tamu.edu,
phone 845-7364, fax 845-6077) by Monday, January 8.  

The guidelines from the Dean of Faculties for these biographical
sketches are included below.  

Thank you in advance for your help.

Dean of Faculties Guidelines for Biographical Paragraphs 

!  The paragraph should not exceed 125 words, be a Microsoft Word file
(not .pdf), and should contain the following six pieces of information
(in this order):
	
1)	Candidate's name
2)	Terminal degree, institution where earned, year earned*
3)	Year they joined the Texas A&M faculty
4)	Area(s) of Specialty
5)	A brief outline of his/her contribution to the department in the
areas of teaching, research and service ("bragging points" that
exemplify to the public the quality of our faculty and contributions
they are making).
6)	Any notable awards or honors

To avoid having our office edit the paragraphs, please closely follow
the format above and do not exceed the word limit.  Know that we will do
our best to include all key information about the candidate, but
paragraphs submitted for the booklet are subject to editorial changes at
the discretion of this office, or we may need to send it back to you
with instructions for further edits.   

*PLEASE NOTE:  For the  College of Science, we  also includes
postdoctoral positions and previous faculty appointments.  

